>> title: Bhuna
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, indian, dry, tomato, curry
>> counters: Curry House, One Pot
>> aka: bhoona, chicken bhuna, bhuna gosht, bhoona gosht, bhunna
>> pairs-with: onion-tomato-masala, chapati, pilau-rice
>> servings: 4
>> time: 55 min

>> step: sear 6 min, until it takes colour
Sear @boneless chicken thighs{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; cut in 2-in pieces) in @ghee{3%Tbs}(42 g) in a wide #heavy pan{} over high heat ~sear{6%min}, until the pieces have colour on two sides.

>> step: fry in 5 min
Fry @onion-tomato masala{1 1/2%cup}(360 g; the base recipe) into @&(~1)seared chicken{} ~fry{5%min}.

>> step: bloom 30 sec off the heat
Bloom @ground cumin{2%tsp}, @ground coriander{2%tsp}, @Kashmiri chile powder{2%tsp} and @garam masala{1%tsp} in @&(~1)pan{} off the heat ~stir{30%sec}.

>> step: fry down 20 min, until the oil breaks out at the sides
Fry @&(~1)curry{} down with @tomato paste{1%Tbs}(16 g), @water{1/4%cup}(60 mL) and @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} ~fry{20%min}, scraping the pan and letting it stick and be scraped again, until the water has gone and a clear ring of oil stands at the sides.

>> step: toss through off the heat
Toss @cilantro{3%Tbs}(chopped), @green chile{1}(slit) and @lemon juice{2%tsp} through @&(~1)bhuna{} off the heat.

The frying-down is the dish. Twenty minutes of it and not five.
